Derived material and where it comes from. All links are permalinks to tag v1.0.3-beta18
of apache/devlake (https://github.com/apache/devlake/blob/v1.0.3-beta18/<path>#L<n>):

1. Table shapes (tests/schema_mysql.sql). Column names and types of the tables
   accounts, pull_requests, pull_request_comments and pull_request_assignees were
   written from the gorm struct tags in:
     backend/core/models/domainlayer/code/pull_request.go
     backend/core/models/domainlayer/code/pull_request_comment.go
     backend/core/models/domainlayer/code/pull_request_assignees.go
     backend/core/models/domainlayer/crossdomain/account.go
     backend/core/models/domainlayer/domainlayer.go
   Only the columns used here are created. The source line of each column is
   written next to it in the file. The Go files were read with the GitHub API;
   apache/devlake is not cloned and no Go code is included.

2. Median method (sql/mysql/agent_review_burden.sql). The median is the largest
   value among rows whose percent_rank() is 0.5 or less, the method used by the
   existing DevLake Grafana dashboards: the pattern
   "max(days_deployed) as median_number_of_deployment_days_per_week" with
   "ranks <= 0.5" in
   https://github.com/apache/devlake/blob/v1.0.3-beta18/grafana/dashboards/mysql/DORA.json#L236

3. First human reaction (sql/mysql/agent_review_burden.sql). The author-exclusion
   condition "pr.author_id IS NULL OR pr.author_id = '' OR comment.account_id != pr.author_id"
   is adapted from the DevLake change lead time calculator, and the bot exclusion
   follows its "COALESCE(acc2.is_bot, false) = false":
   https://github.com/apache/devlake/blob/v1.0.3-beta18/backend/plugins/dora/tasks/change_lead_time_calculator.go#L252-L253

4. How reviews are stored (type REVIEW, status = GitHub review state, no time for
   a review without a submit time) is read from
   https://github.com/apache/devlake/blob/v1.0.3-beta18/backend/plugins/github/tasks/pr_review_convertor.go#L91-L96
   The SQL relies on this behaviour; it does not copy the code.

5. Unsent (PENDING) reviews. DevLake drops them when it extracts reviews (REST:
   https://github.com/apache/devlake/blob/v1.0.3-beta18/backend/plugins/github/tasks/pr_review_extractor.go#L72
   GraphQL:
   https://github.com/apache/devlake/blob/v1.0.3-beta18/backend/plugins/github_graphql/tasks/pr_extractor.go#L101 ).
   The condition in the SQL that removes them is a safeguard, not the main filter.

6. Bot flag. DevLake sets accounts.is_bot when the GitHub user type is "Bot" or the
   login ends in "[bot]":
   https://github.com/apache/devlake/blob/v1.0.3-beta18/backend/plugins/github/tasks/account_convertor.go#L150

7. Test database settings (tests/run_u1.py). The test MySQL is started with
   --character-set-server=utf8mb4 --collation-server=utf8mb4_bin, the options in
   https://github.com/apache/devlake/blob/v1.0.3-beta18/docker-compose-dev-mysql.yml#L33

8. Commit tables (tests/schema_mysql.sql, added with U2). Column names and types of
   pull_request_commits and commits were written from the gorm struct tags in:
     backend/core/models/domainlayer/code/pull_request_commit.go
     backend/core/models/domainlayer/code/commit.go
   Only the columns used are created; the source line of each column is written next
   to it. No Go code is included.

9. First commit and first reviewer (sql/mysql/ai_impact_parity.sql). The first commit of
   a pull request is the one with the smallest commit_authored_date, as in
   batchFetchFirstCommits, and the reviewer conditions follow the first-review query,
   both in
   https://github.com/apache/devlake/blob/v1.0.3-beta18/backend/plugins/dora/tasks/change_lead_time_calculator.go
   (the first-commit query is around line 206 and the first-review query around line 248
   of the original file).

10. The Grafana screen (U5: dashboards/, tools/build_dashboard.py, tools/grafana_install.py). The shape of
   the dashboard json follows (a text panel, then rows; `"timezone": "utc"`; the data source
   `{"type": "mysql", "uid": "devlake-mysql-api"}`), and the fields of the provider file dashboards/provisioning/ai-impact.yml
   follow. One thing is copied: the query of the variable `repo_id` (`select concat(name, '--', id) as text from repos where
   id like 'gitlab%'`) and its regex /^(?<text>.*)--(?<value>.*)$/ from Gitlab.json, with `gitlab%` changed to `github%`.
   No panel is copied. Sources:
     grafana/dashboards/mysql/Gitlab.json
     grafana/dashboards/mysql/engineering-throughput-and-cycle-time.json
     grafana/provisioning/dashboards/dashboard.yml
     grafana/scripts/entrypoint.sh (the data source uid)
     grafana/Dockerfile (the provider path /etc/grafana/dashboards, not used by this repo)
